From 18f4fabb3c83c0dd3e57b1295efb4b14729b6395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:52:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/xenos: invalidate exact texture ranges instead of
 all of DRAM

Before every draw Xenos invalidated the GPU caches over all of DRAM, and that
doesn't reliably reach the texture cache: dEQP uniform_api cases that sample
a cube map (a linear texture the CPU writes into a recycled BO) sampled
stale texels after other cases, and four fbo.render cases failed the same
way. Waiting for the whole GPU before CPU maps only hid it, by splitting
batches.

Invalidate exact ranges, as libxenon does: vertex and index buffers before
every draw, a texture or restored render target only when the CPU wrote it
or it got a new BO since its last invalidate (resolves already invalidate
their destination). Drop the whole-GPU wait before CPU maps.
XENOS_FULL_INVAL=1 brings back the all-of-DRAM invalidate per draw.

